  "response": "Based on the provided context, the field of the promptfoo HTTP provider that transforms the API response is `transformResponse`. This field is used to specify how the response from the API should be reshaped or transformed before it is evaluated by promptfoo.\n\nFor example, in the context provided:\n\n```yaml\nproviders:\n  - id: https\n    config:\n      url: https://your-app.example.com/api/chat\n      method: POST\n      headers:\n        Content-Type: application/json\n      body:\n        prompt: '{{prompt}}'\n      transformResponse: file://./transforms/guardrail-response.mjs\n```\n\nHere, `transformResponse` is used to reference a JavaScript file (`file://./transforms/guardrail-response.mjs`) that defines how the response should be transformed. Similarly, in the A2A provider example:\n\n```yaml\nproviders:\n  - id: a2a:https://agent.example.com/a2a/v1\n    config:\n      transformResponse: |\n        {\n          output: text,\n          metadata: { taskId: context.task?.id, mode: context.mode }\n        }\n```\n\n`transformResponse` is used to specify a JavaScript expression that reshapes the response. \n\nIn summary, the `transformResponse` field is responsible for defining the transformation logic for API responses in promptfoo.",
